        "question": {
          ":question/id": "bcde8b5b-7c69-5a22-9c9f-f19febb8b865",
          ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-4\\left(-x-3\\right)+3x-3=-2\\left(-3x-4\\right)+x+1$\n\n- **II.** $4\\left(2x-2\\right)+x+3=4\\left(3x-3\\right)-4x-1$\n\n- **III.** $2\\left(3x+3\\right)-4x+4=-2\\left(x-3\\right)+4x+4$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\left(-x-3\\right)+3x-3 & =-2\\left(-3x-4\\right)+x+1 \\\\ \\left(-4\\right)\\cdot\\left(-1x\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\\cdot\\left(-3\\right)+3x-3 & =\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot\\left(-3x\\right)+\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot\\left(-4\\right)+x+1 \\\\ 4x+12+3x-3 & =6x+8+x+1 \\\\ 7x+9 & =7x+9 \\\\ 7x+9-7x & =7x+9-7x \\\\ 9 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-4\\left(-x-3\\right)+3x-3=-2\\left(-3x-4\\right)+x+1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\left(2x-2\\right)+x+3 & =4\\left(3x-3\\right)-4x-1 \\\\ \\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(2x\\right)+\\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(-2\\right)+x+3 & =\\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(3x\\right)+\\left(4\\right)\\cdot\\left(-3\\right)-4x-1 \\\\ 8x-8+x+3 & =12x-12-4x-1 \\\\ 9x-5 & =8x-13 \\\\ 9x-5-8x & =8x-13-8x \\\\ x-5 & =-13 \\\\ x-5+5 & =-13+5 \\\\ x & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $4\\left(2x-2\\right)+x+3=4\\left(3x-3\\right)-4x-1$ has the unique solution $x=-8.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\left(3x+3\\right)-4x+4 & =-2\\left(x-3\\right)+4x+4 \\\\ \\left(2\\right)\\cdot\\left(3x\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\cdot\\left(3\\right)-4x+4 & =\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot\\left(1x\\right)+\\left(-2\\right)\\cdot\\left(-3\\right)+4x+4 \\\\ 6x+6-4x+4 & =-2x+6+4x+4 \\\\ 2x+10 & =2x+10 \\\\ 2x+10-2x & =2x+10-2x \\\\ 10 & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $2\\left(3x+3\\right)-4x+4=-2\\left(x-3\\right)+4x+4$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
